=== P18.8 FIRST FAILURE, PRESERVED VERBATIM (CLAUDE.md 1.5) ===
date: 2026-10-02T01:17:08Z

A REAL DEFECT IN THE DEVICE CODE, found by control N11.

The device status was LAST-WRITE-WINS. A state with T = -5 was correctly refused, but the
reason reported was NonFiniteEnergy (12) -- a DOWNSTREAM CONSEQUENCE -- where the CPU, which
throws at the FIRST invalid thing, reports NonPositiveTemperature (2), the ROOT CAUSE.

WHY THAT IS A GATE FAILURE AND NOT COSMETIC: E11 requires the DECISION AND THE REASON to
agree, because two backends rejecting the same state for different reasons is a divergence
in the admissible set. G9 asks for 'the same first-offending cell'. A consequence masking a
cause is exactly that divergence.

